    "q-36987": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36987",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡z$ that passes through the point $P(4,3,e).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4,3,e) & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡e=\\sqrt{25}-1=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=4.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡z & =4 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z \\\\ {e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z} \\\\ {e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4} & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(4,3,e)$ is the surface $z={e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
